WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.842
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.112 --> 00:08.864
[theme music playing]

3
00:46.694 --> 00:50.781
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

4
00:50.906 --> 00:52.491
[theme music concludes]

5
00:52.616 --> 00:53.450
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS, INCIDENTS,

6
00:53.576 --> 00:54.410
AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

7
00:54.535 --> 00:55.369
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

8
00:55.494 --> 00:56.370
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

9
00:56.495 --> 00:58.205
[tender music playing]

10
01:47.671 --> 01:49.131
[music swells]

11
02:15.783 --> 02:16.867
[tender music concludes]

12
02:18.452 --> 02:20.037
You can return it now.

13
02:20.162 --> 02:22.331
[mid-tempo music playing over restaurant speakers]

14
02:28.295 --> 02:29.546
I get what's going on.

15
02:30.464 --> 02:32.174
I won't go back to him, so give it back.

16
02:40.015 --> 02:41.225
Break up with that guy.

17
02:43.352 --> 02:45.020
We have no chance, why bother?

18
02:45.813 --> 02:47.314
If you can read the room, you know.

19
02:48.273 --> 02:51.235
Between the two of them, there's no space for us.

20
02:52.069 --> 02:53.570
[inhales deeply]

21
02:53.696 --> 02:56.281
-So I think-- -You really do love Mi-do.

22
02:59.368 --> 03:00.786
I thought you weren't serious then.

23
03:02.579 --> 03:03.831
I thought you were crazy.

24
03:07.084 --> 03:08.419
Let's form an alliance.

25
03:10.671 --> 03:13.173
You like Namgung, and I like Mi-do.

26
03:14.174 --> 03:15.592
But the deadline is one month.

27
03:16.343 --> 03:17.720
How about a strategic approach?

28
03:19.179 --> 03:20.639
What is your plan exactly?

29
03:20.764 --> 03:23.434
A FEW DAYS AGO

30
03:23.600 --> 03:25.185
Here's what I was thinking.

31
03:25.310 --> 03:26.770
Go on an overnight.

32
03:26.895 --> 03:28.439
Business travel, whatever it takes.

33
03:29.898 --> 03:30.983
Nothing even has to occur.

34
03:31.734 --> 03:33.402
So just go.

35
03:34.945 --> 03:37.239
Just knowing that makes humans nervous.

36
03:37.781 --> 03:38.782
Really mad.

37
03:40.242 --> 03:41.160
And suspicious.

38
03:43.037 --> 03:46.749
All we need is to create a tiny spark to break their trust.

39
03:47.082 --> 03:47.916
[snaps fingers]

40
03:48.042 --> 03:49.293
If we do that, we'll succeed.

41
03:49.418 --> 03:50.294
No way.

42
03:53.297 --> 03:55.966
I suppose you aren't serious about being Namgung's girlfriend.

43
03:57.634 --> 04:01.263
Truth is, when you love someone, you'd do even worse than this.

44
04:02.139 --> 04:03.849
Gladly, without a second thought.

45
04:06.351 --> 04:07.394
That's what you do.

46
04:07.978 --> 04:10.147
Out of everyone, you're the one who isn't serious.

47
04:10.647 --> 04:11.774
[scoffs] Seriously.

48
04:11.899 --> 04:15.736
I hate you, and I feel total repulsion toward you.

49
04:18.072 --> 04:20.324
Since the person I love suffered thanks to you,

50
04:20.991 --> 04:22.242
and because of you,

51
04:23.035 --> 04:25.079
at this very moment, he's still suffering.

52
04:25.746 --> 04:27.706
-[gentle music playing] -[Su-a] I'm begging you.

53
04:28.999 --> 04:30.793
Ms. Lee and you should end things.

54
04:32.336 --> 04:33.420
Stop messing with her.

55
04:34.463 --> 04:35.714
That's all I'm asking.

56
04:40.135 --> 04:41.095
Fair enough.

57
04:41.220 --> 04:42.554
I get how you felt back then.

58
04:43.680 --> 04:45.224
So I'll be ending things with her.

59
04:46.558 --> 04:50.104
But still, it seems like you've had a change of heart.

60
04:50.479 --> 04:51.772
[music rises]

61
04:56.443 --> 04:57.361
Stop it.

62
04:58.654 --> 05:00.572
You're only making it harder on Namgung.

63
05:01.073 --> 05:01.949
Can't you see that?

64
05:02.074 --> 05:03.158
I know.

65
05:04.743 --> 05:05.577
Although…

66
05:07.871 --> 05:09.998
he shouldn't suffer because of your behavior.

67
05:11.125 --> 05:13.127
And I hate that Miss Lee is the reason he's hurting.

68
05:14.503 --> 05:20.425
My original goal for the month was to give him the greatest happiness.

69
05:22.302 --> 05:23.512
But that's changed.

70
05:25.848 --> 05:27.641
I want to make him happy forever.

71
05:29.226 --> 05:33.564
All I want is to keep him blissful for the rest of our lives.

72
05:37.901 --> 05:38.861
[gentle music concludes]

73
05:49.329 --> 05:50.622
[exhales]

74
05:51.123 --> 05:52.124
[sighs]

75
06:02.176 --> 06:03.135
Namgung.

76
06:05.262 --> 06:06.388
Namgung, look at me.

77
06:09.600 --> 06:10.601
I'm right here.

78
06:20.194 --> 06:21.236
[tender music playing]

79
06:33.248 --> 06:37.961
Surely you know how much pain and misery I feel right now.

80
06:39.338 --> 06:40.505
But Namgung…

81
06:42.549 --> 06:43.759
I do know…

82
06:46.678 --> 06:49.056
how sorry you must be feeling about everything.

83
06:51.391 --> 06:53.518
How deeply angry you are at yourself.

84
06:55.520 --> 06:58.815
How you hate this and how you are suffering.

85
07:02.110 --> 07:03.153
I know that too.

86
07:05.822 --> 07:07.282
I'm pretty aware of all that.

87
07:17.125 --> 07:18.168
I know it's my fault.

88
07:20.504 --> 07:22.256
I have no one to blame but myself.

89
07:24.091 --> 07:25.342
This is all my own doing.

90
07:27.928 --> 07:29.429
[music rises]

91
07:29.554 --> 07:33.392
[Mi-do] I was so arrogant and vile that I caused all this.

92
07:35.269 --> 07:36.895
You didn't do anything wrong.

93
07:38.397 --> 07:39.690
I know it's my fault.

94
07:41.858 --> 07:43.527
Mi-do, you're being unfair.

95
07:44.903 --> 07:46.697
-If you keep doing this-- -[Mi-do] Namgung.

96
07:48.615 --> 07:50.826
I finally grew up, I guess, right?

97
07:59.835 --> 08:01.086
[exhales deeply]

98
08:06.883 --> 08:08.427
Let's not stop now.

99
08:10.846 --> 08:14.683
No matter what, let's see this through.

100
08:16.810 --> 08:18.395
Our month is almost up.

101
08:19.563 --> 08:20.605
So let's do it

102
08:21.773 --> 08:22.816
without looking back.

103
08:24.151 --> 08:25.485
Let's finish this month.

104
08:29.656 --> 08:30.574
Hmm?

105
08:39.416 --> 08:40.876
[sighs deeply]

106
08:48.592 --> 08:49.801
[exhales deeply]

107
08:52.054 --> 08:55.932
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

108
08:56.058 --> 09:00.395
WHO WILL WE BE WITH IN TEN YEARS?

109
09:00.520 --> 09:01.938
[tender music concludes]

110
09:02.064 --> 09:06.234
YEAR 2007

111
09:06.360 --> 09:07.903
[young Namgung panting]

112
09:13.283 --> 09:15.285
[students chattering]

113
09:25.670 --> 09:27.214
Is our homeroom teacher insane?

114
09:27.547 --> 09:29.508
Twenty laps outside in this weather?

115
09:32.844 --> 09:33.678
It was you.

116
09:34.596 --> 09:36.765
You're the one who keyed their car, am I right?

117
09:37.557 --> 09:39.142
It was your revenge for that F.

118
09:41.436 --> 09:42.521
[sighs]

119
09:44.022 --> 09:46.400
Namgung is so loyal, you know?

120
09:49.945 --> 09:52.489
[panting]

121
09:55.492 --> 09:57.911
[gentle Korean song playing through earphones]

122
10:22.352 --> 10:23.478
What are you doing?

123
10:24.646 --> 10:25.605
Where's the ninth?

124
10:25.730 --> 10:26.606
Volume nine?

125
10:26.731 --> 10:27.691
[scoffs]

126
10:30.819 --> 10:32.070
[chair scrapes]

127
10:50.380 --> 10:51.798
It was the teacher's fault.

128
10:53.175 --> 10:55.469
They lost my assignment and gave me an F.

129
10:58.597 --> 10:59.598
Are you stupid?

130
10:59.723 --> 11:00.807
Why raise your hand?

131
11:01.933 --> 11:03.643
Did you expect me to thank ya?

132
11:05.479 --> 11:07.272
Why would you run 20 laps?

133
11:07.772 --> 11:11.234
Do you remember when Yeong-do almost torched that rib restaurant

134
11:11.359 --> 11:13.862
and they made you clean for an entire month? I know it all.

135
11:15.947 --> 11:19.576
You paid for Wan-do's swim lessons, and you even bought his swimsuit.

136
11:21.495 --> 11:22.829
Stop living like that.

137
11:23.330 --> 11:25.123
People will walk all over you.

138
11:25.248 --> 11:26.750
Why do you keep doing that?

139
11:31.421 --> 11:32.506
You have no idea?

140
11:33.965 --> 11:35.383
You don't know why I did it?

141
11:36.218 --> 11:37.260
You really don't know?

142
11:38.762 --> 11:39.679
No.

143
11:41.223 --> 11:42.140
I don't know.

144
11:43.141 --> 11:44.976
Then I guess it's better you stay clueless.

145
11:46.061 --> 11:46.937
[scoffs]

146
11:47.479 --> 11:49.439
Fine, I'll keep living like this.

147
11:49.814 --> 11:51.441
I'll stay childish my whole life.

148
11:53.401 --> 11:55.695
I'll never be a pushover like you are.

149
11:59.199 --> 12:00.617
[soft, somber music playing]

150
12:23.682 --> 12:25.934
[man] Park Su-a, for breach of trade secrets,

151
12:26.059 --> 12:26.977
code of ethics violations,

152
12:27.102 --> 12:28.562
and suspected bribery,

153
12:28.687 --> 12:31.064
is suspended while the inquiry is still pending,

154
12:31.189 --> 12:33.358
but will report to work as normal.

155
12:34.150 --> 12:35.986
[soft, somber music concludes]

156
12:47.414 --> 12:48.957
Can you type this?

157
12:49.082 --> 12:50.083
It's an order.

158
12:50.208 --> 12:52.419
You mean the sensory evaluation sheets?

159
12:53.837 --> 12:56.047
Uh, why bother when an OCR scan can do it?

160
12:56.798 --> 12:59.384
Or organize tickets instead?

161
13:02.304 --> 13:03.346
[sighs]

162
13:04.014 --> 13:05.390
[mid-tempo music playing]

163
13:05.515 --> 13:08.310
[Sang-hun] TF Team 3 will be disbanded soon.

164
13:09.477 --> 13:10.729
I'm sorry, I can't do anything else.

165
13:17.068 --> 13:18.194
Don't talk to me.

166
13:19.237 --> 13:20.196
Don't even look at me.

167
13:22.282 --> 13:26.786
Our little coup failed, so now it's every man for himself.

168
13:29.205 --> 13:31.541
I'll only take the blame for disposal.

169
13:32.709 --> 13:36.129
So everything you did, you did it on your own, right?

170
13:36.921 --> 13:38.965
It has absolutely nothing to do with me.

171
13:44.471 --> 13:45.597
[mid-tempo music concludes]

172
13:55.023 --> 13:56.066
[sighs]

173
14:02.405 --> 14:03.698
SCRAP PAPER BIN

174
14:08.161 --> 14:09.079
Take them out.

175
14:11.122 --> 14:12.248
Do it and put them back.

176
14:14.042 --> 14:14.876
No way.

177
14:22.008 --> 14:22.842
[sighs]

178
14:23.343 --> 14:25.220
You know Jeong and Seok went to Thailand?

179
14:25.804 --> 14:26.930
They're not suspended at home.

180
14:27.055 --> 14:28.223
They're on vacation.

181
14:28.348 --> 14:29.349
Director Yoon, too.

182
14:29.891 --> 14:30.850
So what?

183
14:31.476 --> 14:32.977
Take time off and go to Thailand, too.

184
14:33.645 --> 14:35.980
You're not penalized yet, so you can take paid time off.

185
14:36.106 --> 14:37.023
You've got days.

186
14:37.440 --> 14:38.608
That's not the issue.

187
14:43.405 --> 14:44.531
People will return soon.

188
14:45.240 --> 14:46.825
If they see you talking with me, you'll become--

189
14:46.950 --> 14:48.118
Get your typing done.

190
14:49.202 --> 14:50.537
I'll stay right next to you.

191
14:51.663 --> 14:53.790
-Why would you-- -Lunch break is over.

192
14:54.332 --> 14:55.333
Everybody's coming.

193
14:56.501 --> 14:57.836
Want to make things hard for me?

194
15:08.304 --> 15:13.143
[colleagues chattering indistinctly]

195
15:27.949 --> 15:29.033
[Se-young] It's not CGI.

196
15:29.159 --> 15:31.119
Shot 52 seconds a day for four days.

197
15:31.244 --> 15:33.246
-Are you sure it's not CGI? -I swear it.

198
15:33.371 --> 15:35.540
If I go and check and it turns out you lied, you're dead.

199
15:35.665 --> 15:36.791
[sighs wearily]

200
15:36.916 --> 15:39.127
There's no way any studio would let you shoot a sunset

201
15:39.252 --> 15:40.253
for four days straight.

202
15:40.378 --> 15:41.671
I know. Of course I bluffed.

203
15:41.796 --> 15:43.423
[gasps] You're completely nuts.

204
15:43.548 --> 15:45.133
I wrote lines and shot scenes,

205
15:45.258 --> 15:47.218
then cut it all and kept the sunset.

206
15:47.343 --> 15:48.511
-[gasps] -[Se-young] I know.

207
15:48.636 --> 15:49.596
I'm a genius.

208
15:49.721 --> 15:51.014
[groans] So annoying.

209
15:51.306 --> 15:52.891
It's a fair point. Can't argue that.

210
15:53.016 --> 15:54.017
I'm a genius.

211
15:54.559 --> 15:55.810
Sure, but just a little.

212
15:57.729 --> 15:59.355
Tell me, how was the ending done?

213
15:59.481 --> 16:00.523
The window in that month?

214
16:00.648 --> 16:01.858
-Mi-do? -Yeah?

215
16:01.983 --> 16:03.276
Only you get to know this.

216
16:03.401 --> 16:04.402
Uh-huh.

217
16:05.195 --> 16:06.780
I only saw it in the rough cut.

218
16:06.905 --> 16:08.782
-[gasps] Really? -[Se-young chuckles]

219
16:08.907 --> 16:10.867
The editor added it for impact at the end.

220
16:10.992 --> 16:12.660
Whoa, I can't believe it.

221
16:12.786 --> 16:14.537
Now tell me, how'd you shoot that airport scene?

222
16:14.662 --> 16:17.207
For that shot, I got the drone and lighting teams at the same hour--

223
16:17.332 --> 16:18.541
You guys own this place or what?

224
16:21.836 --> 16:22.754
Keep the volume down.

225
16:24.255 --> 16:25.548
-[weary music playing] -[Tae-seung] Oh.

226
16:26.257 --> 16:30.094
My date ghosted me today, so I'm in a terrible mood.

227
16:32.597 --> 16:33.598
Just keep it quiet.

228
16:34.182 --> 16:35.517
We're really sorry.

229
16:42.857 --> 16:43.691
Hey,

230
16:44.692 --> 16:46.528
I heard… He said date, right?

231
16:47.612 --> 16:49.864
I think… I think he swings my way.

232
16:51.658 --> 16:52.826
Was that flirting?

233
16:52.951 --> 16:54.577
He kept staring a few minutes ago.

234
16:54.702 --> 16:58.581
Hey, if you're wearing knockoffs, get high-grade ones.

235
16:59.374 --> 17:00.291
Come on.

236
17:00.416 --> 17:01.918
The exact moment you get paid,

237
17:02.043 --> 17:04.087
just go to the store and buy the real thing.

238
17:04.712 --> 17:05.797
Chin up.

239
17:05.922 --> 17:06.923
Good.

240
17:08.591 --> 17:09.717
Is it that obvious?

241
17:09.843 --> 17:11.135
Duh! Of course it is.

242
17:15.849 --> 17:16.850
Oh, he's gorgeous.

243
17:16.975 --> 17:18.643
[chuckles] What is with you?

244
17:24.941 --> 17:26.192
Miss Lee, don't overdo it.

245
17:26.317 --> 17:27.402
[weary music concludes]

246
17:28.278 --> 17:30.738
You're already a mess over Namgung and Park Su-a.

247
17:32.365 --> 17:33.449
Don't push yourself.

248
17:34.409 --> 17:36.244
Are you in any position to celebrate others?

249
17:36.369 --> 17:37.370
Why?

250
17:38.121 --> 17:39.122
Am I pushing myself?

251
17:39.247 --> 17:40.290
Aren't you?

252
17:40.415 --> 17:42.208
Hmm. Not at all.

253
17:50.341 --> 17:53.386
[slurring] Okay, Mi-do, where did I leave off again?

254
17:54.345 --> 17:55.305
Oh.

255
17:56.723 --> 17:57.891
The scene where he falls,

256
17:58.266 --> 18:00.018
-that was-- -Tak Jackson.

257
18:02.520 --> 18:03.855
Do you recall those days?

258
18:06.232 --> 18:09.819
Three years ago, when Park Jae-young's casting fell through

259
18:10.612 --> 18:13.156
the studio told you to give up with the whole thing.

260
18:14.198 --> 18:15.116
And your words were…

261
18:16.659 --> 18:18.411
Oh! That's right.

262
18:19.537 --> 18:22.540
That I'd quit movies and do YouTube videos.

263
18:22.665 --> 18:26.544
Film industry, look out! Masked Mouse is trashing you.

264
18:26.669 --> 18:29.672
Right, you said we'd do that. [laughs]

265
18:30.256 --> 18:33.301
[laughing]

266
18:35.053 --> 18:37.347
-No? -"The story needs to be written."

267
18:39.265 --> 18:41.225
"I'm dying to make it."

268
18:43.645 --> 18:44.979
"Make all of this true."

269
18:45.855 --> 18:48.232
You said all of that, don't you remember?

270
18:49.067 --> 18:50.360
"This movie will get made."

271
18:53.529 --> 18:54.739
I knew it right then.

272
18:56.699 --> 18:58.034
He'll make it, this idiot.

273
19:00.078 --> 19:03.581
This is what it means to be a director.

274
19:05.375 --> 19:06.668
He should be making movies.

275
19:07.293 --> 19:08.586
[laughs]

276
19:09.712 --> 19:13.132
[laughing]

277
19:13.925 --> 19:15.259
[soft music playing]

278
19:18.262 --> 19:20.723
I mean, calling it a Lord of the Rings knockoff?

279
19:20.848 --> 19:22.392
Just ignore them. Screw that.

280
19:23.017 --> 19:26.104
Don't listen to them saying you had no real competition.

281
19:26.229 --> 19:29.190
Tell them to cut the bullshit about getting lucky.

282
19:29.315 --> 19:30.733
Come on, it wasn't just the cast.

283
19:31.234 --> 19:32.235
I know.

284
19:32.860 --> 19:34.070
[Mi-do] Listen to me, okay?

285
19:36.155 --> 19:40.284
It worked out because you did a great job.

286
19:42.245 --> 19:43.788
Because you didn't quit.

287
19:45.373 --> 19:48.084
You are the one who made it.

288
19:50.503 --> 19:51.713
Hmm?

289
19:59.846 --> 20:00.930
Luc Mi-do.

290
20:01.222 --> 20:04.600
You know, when it comes to races, a really good runner

291
20:05.476 --> 20:09.397
only sprints in the last two kilometers to avoid getting too tired.

292
20:10.064 --> 20:11.524
Mmm.

293
20:11.649 --> 20:13.693
But your race isn't over.

294
20:13.818 --> 20:14.986
This isn't the last two K.

295
20:16.362 --> 20:17.864
And that's why it's so tough.

296
20:19.323 --> 20:20.450
Hang in there, all right?

297
20:20.742 --> 20:21.743
Really?

298
20:21.868 --> 20:23.536
You call that comforting?

299
20:26.748 --> 20:27.915
I'm sorry.

300
20:28.041 --> 20:29.667
That was a bad example, huh?

301
20:29.792 --> 20:32.211
[laughs]

302
20:33.880 --> 20:36.883
[sobbing]

303
20:40.803 --> 20:44.348
[sobbing]

304
20:50.646 --> 20:54.817
-[sobbing] -[Se-yeong sobbing] Mi-do.

305
21:01.324 --> 21:02.742
[soft music concludes]

306
21:05.369 --> 21:06.621
Can I buy you dinner?

307
21:13.127 --> 21:15.213
Times like this, you need to eat well.

308
21:15.838 --> 21:18.174
Food is 80% of what keeps you going.

309
21:21.010 --> 21:22.011
Su-a.

310
21:24.972 --> 21:26.182
Sweetheart.

311
21:27.850 --> 21:29.227
Deok-sun.

312
21:32.605 --> 21:33.689
I want to buy you dinner.

313
21:35.316 --> 21:36.776
Let's get something good to eat.

314
21:39.112 --> 21:40.196
I want to hear it now.

315
21:42.698 --> 21:44.158
You said ten seconds of eye contact,

316
21:44.700 --> 21:46.619
and you'd tell me what Miss Lee doesn't know.

317
21:50.081 --> 21:51.040
I know it's childish.

318
21:51.999 --> 21:53.543
I hate doing it, although…

319
21:53.668 --> 21:55.920
[Namgung] The reason I never told Mi-do that…

320
21:57.547 --> 21:59.340
is because I love her more than anything.

321
22:01.801 --> 22:03.219
It's humiliating for me.

322
22:06.264 --> 22:09.350
So I never wanted her to find out about it, that's why.

323
22:11.477 --> 22:13.396
I can't tell you about it at all.

324
22:19.318 --> 22:20.361
You're a coward.

325
22:22.780 --> 22:24.448
You're being really cowardly about this.

326
22:24.574 --> 22:25.575
I know.

327
22:26.409 --> 22:27.618
So I'm buying you something good.

328
22:28.619 --> 22:29.620
What do you want?

329
22:31.831 --> 22:32.665
No thanks.

330
22:34.792 --> 22:35.710
I'm gonna cook for us.

331
22:37.461 --> 22:39.046
I'll cook you something really, really good.

332
22:42.508 --> 22:43.342
Sure.

333
22:44.802 --> 22:45.970
[Su-a breathing deeply]

334
22:46.095 --> 22:47.430
[quirky music playing]

335
22:50.766 --> 22:51.767
[squeals]

336
23:35.186 --> 23:37.146
There are great meal kits these days.

337
23:38.522 --> 23:40.399
Just before your boyfriend arrives,

338
23:40.650 --> 23:42.777
ditch the packaging to destroy the evidence.

339
23:43.861 --> 23:46.322
Put the chopped scallions and minced garlic into containers

340
23:46.447 --> 23:47.531
and pretend they're yours.

341
23:48.115 --> 23:49.742
Six out of ten will totally buy it,

342
23:49.867 --> 23:53.162
and the other four guys will just play along with that.

343
23:54.622 --> 23:56.874
Try to date one of the six guys who'd buy it.

344
23:57.750 --> 23:59.168
Dense people should date.

345
24:01.254 --> 24:02.296
[Su-a] I don't want to.

346
24:02.421 --> 24:03.256
[quirky music concludes]

347
24:03.714 --> 24:04.924
I'm going to date you.

348
24:09.220 --> 24:10.805
You're starting to fall for me, right?

349
24:11.514 --> 24:13.099
Then keep it going. Go ahead.

350
24:14.267 --> 24:16.519
I know I can make you happier than anyone else.

351
24:18.062 --> 24:19.188
I'm sure I can.

352
24:23.192 --> 24:24.068
You're wrong.

353
24:25.778 --> 24:26.988
You'll be jobless soon.

354
24:27.738 --> 24:29.156
I don't like women with no future.

355
24:29.532 --> 24:30.574
That's a turn-off.

356
24:31.742 --> 24:32.702
[scoffs]

357
24:33.286 --> 24:34.954
Well, my resume can get me anywhere.

358
24:36.455 --> 24:39.542
Once I clear my name at the hearing, I'm stepping down.

359
24:39.667 --> 24:40.793
And in two months, I will--

360
24:40.918 --> 24:42.670
You think other companies are free of this?

361
24:45.089 --> 24:46.340
You'll run away as well?

362
24:47.591 --> 24:48.467
Am I wrong?

363
24:49.427 --> 24:53.347
You were right but dismissed, while those in the wrong stand proud.

364
24:54.724 --> 24:57.852
And yet the world keeps turning as if nothing happened,

365
24:57.977 --> 24:59.937
and you just feel full of anger.

366
25:00.479 --> 25:01.731
So you're running away.

367
25:03.274 --> 25:04.942
[gentle Korean pop song playing]

368
25:08.070 --> 25:08.988
Why can't I?

369
25:10.781 --> 25:11.949
It's completely wrong.

370
25:12.867 --> 25:15.036
If I agree, I'm no different from those guys.

371
25:16.329 --> 25:17.538
I don't want to be that way.

372
25:18.539 --> 25:19.707
I refuse that life.

373
25:22.418 --> 25:23.586
Then don't accept it.

374
25:24.670 --> 25:28.841
But if you do, you won't make it to the end of the race.

375
25:30.009 --> 25:32.845
The life ahead of you is 5,000 kilometers long.

376
25:34.597 --> 25:37.892
Yet with all those noble values, convictions, and principles…

377
25:39.727 --> 25:42.021
you won't make it a 100 meters keeping them all.

378
25:43.022 --> 25:44.523
I'm not telling you to break them.

379
25:47.234 --> 25:52.156
If people like you don't exist anymore, it's even better for those guys,

380
25:52.281 --> 25:53.407
and it's unfair.

381
25:56.494 --> 25:57.995
I felt so, so wronged.

382
25:59.955 --> 26:01.415
That made me mad as hell.

383
26:02.708 --> 26:03.667
That's why…

384
26:05.503 --> 26:07.254
instead of destroying, I chose to shape them.

385
26:09.048 --> 26:12.968
I said I could just cut some parts away.

386
26:14.762 --> 26:16.972
I compromised that much with myself.

387
26:20.559 --> 26:21.602
So listen.

388
26:23.270 --> 26:24.605
Let yours be shaped too.

389
26:27.316 --> 26:29.693
Your convictions and your values.

390
26:32.113 --> 26:34.448
If you want to protect them at all, let them be shaped.

391
26:44.875 --> 26:46.335
[gentle Korean pop song concludes]

392
26:53.801 --> 26:55.136
Let's go home now.

393
26:55.261 --> 26:56.345
Not yet.

394
26:57.179 --> 26:58.222
Just one more lap.

395
26:58.681 --> 26:59.932
We've done ten laps already.

396
27:00.307 --> 27:01.183
I'm tired and hurt.

397
27:01.642 --> 27:02.726
Our month is almost over.

398
27:03.394 --> 27:04.311
Can't you just try?

399
27:04.687 --> 27:05.729
Han Tae-seung.

400
27:13.821 --> 27:15.906
[tender music playing]

401
27:16.657 --> 27:19.118
You hugged that director, Tak, or whatever his name was.

402
27:20.286 --> 27:21.370
Let me just have this.

403
27:24.373 --> 27:25.249
You know what?

404
27:26.459 --> 27:30.379
Lee Mi-do, you're a better person than I thought.

405
27:32.923 --> 27:36.594
That's why I think I can let you go.

406
27:38.387 --> 27:39.597
I think I have to.

407
27:44.518 --> 27:45.895
I'll get over you eventually.

408
27:47.229 --> 27:48.772
I swear, I definitely will.

409
27:50.316 --> 27:51.442
Just wait and watch.

410
27:54.570 --> 27:55.613
I will get over you.

411
28:05.789 --> 28:07.208
-[gasps] -[Tae-seung groans]

412
28:09.627 --> 28:10.836
Who are you, you bastard?

413
28:10.961 --> 28:12.004
Huh?

414
28:13.130 --> 28:14.173
Hey, Mi-do, are you crazy?

415
28:14.924 --> 28:16.634
Are you two fucking seeing each other?

416
28:19.136 --> 28:20.012
Say something.

417
28:20.596 --> 28:21.847
Are you involved with him?

418
28:22.348 --> 28:24.767
Are you cheating on Namgung?!

419
28:25.226 --> 28:27.019
Namgung's seeing someone else too.

420
28:27.645 --> 28:28.521
Han Tae-seung.

421
28:28.646 --> 28:31.899
That bastard Namgung is seeing someone else too.

422
28:32.983 --> 28:35.444
[breathing heavily]

423
28:39.490 --> 28:40.574
[tender music concludes]

424
28:40.699 --> 28:41.617
HONDURAS KARAOKE

425
28:41.742 --> 28:43.160
Don't you dare go alone.

426
28:43.911 --> 28:45.663
I'll join you diving this weekend.

427
28:47.748 --> 28:48.832
You were angry, weren't you?

428
28:49.250 --> 28:51.085
Stop acting like a therapist.

429
28:53.045 --> 28:54.964
I'm not angry. I'm just upset.

430
28:57.508 --> 28:58.634
What depth are you?

431
29:02.179 --> 29:03.264
How far down…

432
29:05.182 --> 29:06.016
are you now?

433
29:09.478 --> 29:10.563
[door bell tinkles]

434
29:12.106 --> 29:13.023
Bro!

435
29:13.732 --> 29:14.692
What the fuck?

436
29:14.817 --> 29:15.901
What are you doing?

437
29:17.403 --> 29:18.404
It's not true.

438
29:18.529 --> 29:20.614
[breathing heavily] It's all bullshit, right?

439
29:27.246 --> 29:28.289
Let's talk outside.

440
29:28.414 --> 29:29.290
Why?

441
29:29.665 --> 29:31.667
Are you worried this kid will be shocked?!

442
29:34.295 --> 29:36.714
It's about Sang-su. Just a confusion.

443
29:36.839 --> 29:37.756
He broke up with Mi-do.

444
29:39.466 --> 29:40.301
Yeong.

445
29:40.426 --> 29:43.220
Mi-do is hooking up with that lawyer punk from his army days,

446
29:43.971 --> 29:45.639
and he's dating a younger coworker.

447
29:45.764 --> 29:46.974
Can't be true.

448
29:47.433 --> 29:48.559
That's a lie.

449
29:49.101 --> 29:51.020
Namgung, he's got it all wrong, right?

450
29:52.855 --> 29:54.231
Mi-do has always been crazy.

451
29:54.815 --> 29:56.358
She's never been in her right mind.

452
29:56.984 --> 29:59.737
Then you should have held on to her with everything that you had!

453
29:59.862 --> 30:00.988
Sure.

454
30:01.488 --> 30:02.906
I'm sure Mi-do messed up first.

455
30:03.574 --> 30:05.367
She caused trouble first, obviously.

456
30:05.492 --> 30:06.577
She's capable of that.

457
30:07.620 --> 30:09.288
Still, you had no right to do this.

458
30:09.872 --> 30:11.582
It doesn't even matter what she did.

459
30:12.082 --> 30:13.667
That was completely out of line.

460
30:13.792 --> 30:15.210
Who caused my dad to…

461
30:18.213 --> 30:20.341
[somber music playing]

462
30:24.094 --> 30:25.012
I…

463
30:26.263 --> 30:27.348
I didn't mean that.

464
30:29.558 --> 30:30.601
Wasn't it enough?

465
30:35.105 --> 30:37.107
Was everything I did for you still not enough?

466
30:43.030 --> 30:44.615
The price of your dad's life.

467
30:47.868 --> 30:51.246
I thought I did my best to repay that debt I had with you.

468
30:52.539 --> 30:53.749
-Hey, Namgung. -[grunts]

469
30:58.337 --> 30:59.338
I'm asking you.

470
31:01.048 --> 31:02.007
Answer me.

471
31:06.595 --> 31:07.721
Wasn't it enough?

472
31:15.979 --> 31:17.523
Hiding out behind your relatives.

473
31:19.775 --> 31:21.985
Every day I did it out of guilt.

474
31:23.946 --> 31:25.322
I gave all I had…

475
31:27.408 --> 31:30.452
because I knew I had to pay back the price of your dad's life.

476
31:33.288 --> 31:34.289
You know what?

477
31:36.542 --> 31:38.919
Every single day I was living in hell.

478
31:40.838 --> 31:42.339
Since I survived that day,

479
31:44.091 --> 31:45.384
not a single second,

480
31:46.844 --> 31:50.556
not even for a single second have I been happy!

481
31:50.681 --> 31:51.765
You know that?

482
31:52.141 --> 31:53.225
[inhales harshly]

483
31:56.603 --> 31:57.938
[breathes shakily]

484
31:58.063 --> 31:59.189
[somber music concludes]

485
31:59.314 --> 32:00.774
[door bell tinkles]

486
32:00.899 --> 32:02.359
[melancholic music playing]

487
32:03.193 --> 32:04.278
[exhales deeply]

488
32:05.988 --> 32:07.322
[Mi-do] Dad's death was my fault.

489
32:17.040 --> 32:18.000
That day,

490
32:19.752 --> 32:21.879
our father didn't want to go in the water.

491
32:23.881 --> 32:25.048
I caused a scene…

492
32:26.967 --> 32:28.260
so he went to the rescue.

493
32:30.804 --> 32:32.347
Not because of Namgung.

494
32:33.974 --> 32:35.017
It was my fault.

495
32:38.145 --> 32:39.480
It's my fault dad is dead now.

496
32:57.080 --> 32:58.499
Namgung, I'm sorry.

497
33:01.043 --> 33:02.711
I was such a coward.

498
33:04.171 --> 33:05.506
I hid behind you.

499
33:08.091 --> 33:09.468
For far too long.

500
33:11.011 --> 33:12.179
I hid behind you.

501
33:16.725 --> 33:17.726
Sorry.

502
33:20.020 --> 33:20.854
I'm really…

503
33:21.730 --> 33:23.232
I'm sorry for everything.

504
33:27.319 --> 33:28.654
[exhales sharply]

505
33:40.666 --> 33:44.503
[Yeong-do sobbing softly]

506
33:44.628 --> 33:46.713
[sobbing]

507
33:47.881 --> 33:49.383
[sobbing hysterically]

508
33:50.217 --> 33:51.677
[melancholic music concludes]

509
33:51.802 --> 33:54.012
Namgung won't forgive me, will he?

510
33:55.097 --> 33:56.306
He'll never see me again.

511
33:58.809 --> 34:00.227
That's ridiculous. Don't be silly.

512
34:00.352 --> 34:05.399
[wailing]

513
34:06.733 --> 34:07.818
Wait!

514
34:09.236 --> 34:10.988
Why are you sitting over there?

515
34:11.113 --> 34:12.573
Want to get hit more?

516
34:14.491 --> 34:15.450
Yeah.

517
34:16.827 --> 34:19.454
My injuries won't last four weeks, so I can't sue.

518
34:22.875 --> 34:23.876
I dare ya.

519
34:25.168 --> 34:28.380
That's the only thing that'll finally knock some sense into me.

520
34:28.505 --> 34:31.633
[wailing]

521
34:31.884 --> 34:32.759
[sighs]

522
34:34.094 --> 34:35.679
[wails]

523
34:56.867 --> 35:00.078
Your dad was honored as model firefighter three separate times.

524
35:02.873 --> 35:05.876
Believing he came to the rescue just because you begged…

525
35:08.253 --> 35:10.005
is a huge insult to his legacy.

526
35:12.382 --> 35:16.845
And what I said to Yeong-do earlier, I just got so mad right then.

527
35:20.432 --> 35:22.517
I said it without thinking. It just came out.

528
35:25.479 --> 35:26.855
Yeah, it's true, I felt guilty.

529
35:28.941 --> 35:30.484
And indebted too, but still.

530
35:36.406 --> 35:37.449
The thing is…

531
35:41.745 --> 35:42.704
I'm just…

532
35:45.832 --> 35:47.042
Mi-do, I really did…

533
36:09.398 --> 36:10.482
I know.

534
36:12.192 --> 36:13.527
You are happy, right?

535
36:17.739 --> 36:20.325
It made you happy to do something for my family

536
36:20.450 --> 36:22.703
when we were hurting, right?

537
36:26.790 --> 36:28.041
How could I not know that?

538
36:29.418 --> 36:31.670
I know it all, you dummy.

539
36:34.297 --> 36:35.674
[soft Korean song playing]

540
36:35.799 --> 36:37.467
[young Mi-do] Stop living like that!

541
36:37.592 --> 36:39.219
People will walk all over you!

542
36:46.727 --> 36:49.438
I was happy doing it.

543
36:51.773 --> 36:56.737
I was really happy I could do it for you, so I never felt tired running.

544
36:57.654 --> 36:59.364
I was really happy doing it.

545
37:02.784 --> 37:03.827
I know it, Mi-do.

546
37:04.870 --> 37:06.288
Even I think I'm pretty weird.

547
37:08.540 --> 37:11.168
When I aid someone I care about, I feel stronger.

548
37:12.085 --> 37:15.714
I could even lose everything I have, and I'd still be happy.

549
37:20.677 --> 37:22.220
[song swells]

550
37:23.680 --> 37:27.684
You'll just be called a pushover, and they'll use you.

551
37:28.060 --> 37:29.603
Being used, that's not what it is.

552
37:31.063 --> 37:35.525
I swear to you, that makes me content,

553
37:36.526 --> 37:37.569
you dummy.

554
37:58.048 --> 37:58.965
Namgung.

555
38:01.343 --> 38:03.136
That's exactly who you are.

556
38:05.180 --> 38:07.224
Someone who gives and finds joy in it.

557
38:09.893 --> 38:11.645
And who's happy because of it.

558
38:12.938 --> 38:16.900
People who don't have any idea call that having low self-esteem.

559
38:19.152 --> 38:21.863
They may say you're looking for love desperately.

560
38:23.156 --> 38:24.074
[sniffles]

561
38:27.202 --> 38:28.245
They're all wrong.

562
38:36.586 --> 38:39.214
Because you have more love than anyone.

563
38:44.010 --> 38:49.808
You have so much love that giving it causes you real, real happiness.

564
38:59.359 --> 39:01.945
A pushover isn't a stupid or easy person.

565
39:04.698 --> 39:06.366
They're someone with a lot to give.

566
39:09.035 --> 39:10.954
That's why you give all the time to others,

567
39:11.079 --> 39:12.664
because you have a lot in you.

568
39:13.832 --> 39:15.375
And because you can refill it.

569
39:16.793 --> 39:20.964
You can gladly give away all that love you have.

570
39:24.301 --> 39:25.260
Right?

571
39:33.143 --> 39:35.270
You're a happy pushover.

572
39:39.441 --> 39:40.483
Aren't you?

573
39:52.871 --> 39:53.997
[Namgung] Mi-do.

574
39:55.040 --> 39:56.041
Hmm.

575
39:58.710 --> 40:00.295
Don't grow up, please.

576
40:06.468 --> 40:08.511
Don't grow up, you hear?

577
40:12.182 --> 40:13.266
Don't grow up.

578
40:24.903 --> 40:26.404
[soft Korean song concludes]

579
40:26.529 --> 40:28.865
[humming]

580
40:28.990 --> 40:29.908
QUEENS SALON

581
40:30.033 --> 40:32.535
So tell us, what's Mi-do been up to, huh?

582
40:32.661 --> 40:33.662
Don't.

583
40:34.663 --> 40:36.706
She's marrying Namgung soon, right?

584
40:36.831 --> 40:38.041
That's the goal!

585
40:38.166 --> 40:39.626
Marry a good man, right?

586
40:39.751 --> 40:41.294
Exactly! [chuckles]

587
40:41.419 --> 40:44.130
[woman] Now shush, just read your magazine quietly.

588
41:00.355 --> 41:01.898
[Namgung] Ms. Ma, you wanna get some fresh air?

589
41:06.903 --> 41:08.780
Let's sell these and get some good food.

590
41:09.030 --> 41:10.073
Deal?

591
41:25.463 --> 41:26.423
Working today?

592
41:27.924 --> 41:28.883
Took a half day.

593
41:31.094 --> 41:33.763
On my way to work this morning, the weather was just so nice.

594
41:35.140 --> 41:37.100
So I thought of you and played hooky.

595
41:38.018 --> 41:39.269
That's what I thought too.

596
41:40.437 --> 41:43.690
Rolling perms would be an awful way to spend such a nice day.

597
41:44.399 --> 41:45.317
Stop lying.

598
41:54.534 --> 41:55.410
You know everything.

599
42:00.457 --> 42:01.416
So now what?

600
42:02.292 --> 42:03.585
You won't even try?

601
42:10.467 --> 42:12.052
Trying isn't the hard part.

602
42:13.970 --> 42:15.430
I just feel so awfully sorry.

603
42:17.891 --> 42:19.017
So sorry that…

604
42:22.312 --> 42:23.313
I can't do this.

605
42:27.817 --> 42:28.735
I'm sorry.

606
42:32.572 --> 42:33.531
Hoya.

607
42:34.866 --> 42:37.327
Did you forget what I told you before?

608
42:38.703 --> 42:40.580
Yeong-do is the soft one.

609
42:41.164 --> 42:42.791
Wan-do is the mean one.

610
42:43.958 --> 42:45.335
Mi-do is the kind one.

611
42:47.879 --> 42:49.547
So what kind of guy are you, huh?

612
42:52.592 --> 42:53.551
Hmm.

613
42:57.180 --> 43:01.184
I'll say… the gorgeous one.

614
43:01.810 --> 43:02.769
Don't flatter yourself.

615
43:02.894 --> 43:04.229
[laughs]

616
43:04.729 --> 43:05.980
[chuckles]

617
43:08.942 --> 43:09.984
Hmm.

618
43:12.153 --> 43:13.738
The pathetic one?

619
43:15.907 --> 43:17.200
The heartbreaking one?

620
43:18.660 --> 43:19.536
No?

621
43:21.079 --> 43:22.288
[snaps fingers] I got it.

622
43:23.665 --> 43:24.874
The most hated by you.

623
43:25.708 --> 43:26.709
The one you hate the most,

624
43:27.544 --> 43:29.504
but feel too sorry for to ever truly despise.

625
43:30.130 --> 43:31.089
Am I right?

626
43:32.715 --> 43:33.633
That's not it.

627
43:36.553 --> 43:37.637
The precious one.

628
43:42.725 --> 43:43.852
The one I love most.

629
43:48.606 --> 43:50.150
I remember back then…

630
43:52.152 --> 43:57.323
when you were just a little child, I said such awful things to you,

631
43:57.449 --> 44:01.119
things I could barely utter, and it pressed on me endlessly.

632
44:03.413 --> 44:05.206
The thing is, I was furious.

633
44:06.791 --> 44:09.669
I wondered who was this kid who killed my husband

634
44:09.794 --> 44:12.255
to stay stuck in my heart like a thorn.

635
44:13.214 --> 44:14.591
No matter how I saw it,

636
44:14.716 --> 44:16.926
I thought I had every right to be like that.

637
44:18.386 --> 44:19.929
No matter how young you were,

638
44:20.054 --> 44:23.183
I thought I had the right to take it all out on you.

639
44:27.729 --> 44:29.564
How was I meant to survive that?

640
44:31.649 --> 44:35.111
Without someone to tear into, how was I to survive?

641
44:37.739 --> 44:39.407
That's why I went to see you.

642
44:40.867 --> 44:46.623
I kept thinking of you, of that kid, though not as a thorn anymore.

643
44:47.123 --> 44:48.374
Not out of guilt, either.

644
44:49.292 --> 44:51.377
I believed hating you would make it easier.

645
44:53.129 --> 44:54.923
I figured the moment I saw your face,

646
44:55.590 --> 44:58.009
I might be able to hate you more than I do.

647
44:59.427 --> 45:02.263
-[light music playing] -[breathes deeply]

648
45:02.388 --> 45:04.474
-[girl 1] Thank you, ma'am. -Enjoy your food.

649
45:06.434 --> 45:07.477
[woman1 ] Enjoy, my dear.

650
45:07.602 --> 45:08.770
It's really spicy.

651
45:09.854 --> 45:10.939
Would you like a little?

652
45:13.107 --> 45:14.067
Enjoy your food.

653
45:16.152 --> 45:17.487
Green light. Red light!

654
45:17.612 --> 45:19.697
Green light. Green light. Red light!

655
45:19.822 --> 45:22.200
-Green light. Green light. -[woman 2] Hey, Namgung!

656
45:22.325 --> 45:24.202
[children cheering, laughing]

657
45:24.327 --> 45:25.370
[boy] Wait for me.

658
45:25.495 --> 45:28.456
-[children laughing] -[boy] You're going too fast!

659
45:32.001 --> 45:33.002
[girl 2] Thank you.

660
45:39.217 --> 45:41.886
[curtains rattling]

661
45:42.011 --> 45:45.139
[Ms. Ma] The thing is, you were such a lovely child.

662
45:46.432 --> 45:48.268
I went to find a reason to hate you,

663
45:49.060 --> 45:51.020
but all I saw was how lovely you were.

664
45:55.400 --> 45:57.110
That's why I brought you home.

665
45:58.444 --> 45:59.404
[sniffles]

666
46:02.073 --> 46:03.491
You were a lovely child.

667
46:05.159 --> 46:08.871
Too lovely to leave in a place like that.

668
46:16.129 --> 46:17.130
Hoya,

669
46:18.506 --> 46:21.718
you know, out of everyone in this world,

670
46:21.843 --> 46:23.761
I have the most reason to despite you.

671
46:25.430 --> 46:28.766
So if you were that lovely to me, even at that young age,

672
46:29.851 --> 46:32.604
then there's no doubt you really are a lovely person.

673
46:37.942 --> 46:40.570
That's a thing you can't forget as long as you live.

674
46:45.491 --> 46:46.784
Even in the case…

675
46:47.994 --> 46:51.664
Even if by some chance, you and Mi-do drift away,

676
46:53.666 --> 46:56.044
and you end up all alone again, no matter what…

677
46:58.296 --> 46:59.797
if you keep that in mind,

678
47:00.381 --> 47:03.092
you can still live that good life you've earned.

679
47:05.136 --> 47:08.473
That will get you through the rest of your life, no matter what.

680
47:13.519 --> 47:16.230
I know Mi-do will be all right.

681
47:18.274 --> 47:21.569
My daughter, she's a lot stronger than you can realize.

682
47:24.614 --> 47:27.283
I was too busy scraping by to raise her like that.

683
47:29.285 --> 47:31.162
Thus, you deserve all the credit.

684
47:36.584 --> 47:39.587
You did a wonderful job raising her as a strong girl.

685
47:49.931 --> 47:51.474
[light music concludes]

686
47:59.440 --> 48:00.400
[panting]

687
48:00.525 --> 48:01.693
Is the rumor true?

688
48:02.860 --> 48:03.861
It isn't, right?

689
48:04.112 --> 48:05.321
Just tell me it isn't.

690
48:10.076 --> 48:11.119
It's true.

691
48:11.536 --> 48:14.330
They transferred me to the Tongyeong factory.

692
48:15.289 --> 48:17.250
You can probably stay at headquarters,

693
48:18.000 --> 48:19.836
but I've done this so I know how it goes.

694
48:19.961 --> 48:21.629
I'm not asking that and you know it.

695
48:24.340 --> 48:25.466
You brought it all back?

696
48:26.300 --> 48:27.510
The footage, did you restore it?

697
48:29.762 --> 48:30.763
Yeah.

698
48:30.888 --> 48:32.014
Namgung did it.

699
48:33.141 --> 48:34.600
He's a real tough cookie.

700
48:36.227 --> 48:38.730
That's why he took it to Executive Director Yoon.

701
48:43.359 --> 48:44.569
Namgung did it all.

702
48:46.279 --> 48:50.158
Thanks to him, at the very least, I got sent to Tongyeong.

703
48:50.908 --> 48:52.535
You'll be able to stay right here.

704
48:54.620 --> 48:55.830
[gentle music playing]

705
48:58.583 --> 49:00.460
You've never let me down until now.

706
49:03.421 --> 49:04.464
Restoring that footage…

707
49:06.799 --> 49:08.468
you gave it knowing he could do it?

708
49:08.926 --> 49:12.680
Or should I say, so he wouldn't expose it,

709
49:13.473 --> 49:15.516
but deal with Executive Director Yoon?

710
49:17.977 --> 49:20.813
You knew how broken inside he was when you gave it to him.

711
49:22.064 --> 49:23.649
How could you possibly do that?

712
49:25.443 --> 49:27.153
To him, of all people.

713
49:28.863 --> 49:30.364
How could you possibly do this?

714
49:33.618 --> 49:36.871
After everything he'd been suffering.

715
49:38.206 --> 49:41.334
Because I'm reduced to nothing after all this.

716
49:42.043 --> 49:43.377
I had nothing left to lose.

717
49:46.464 --> 49:47.465
Sorry.

718
49:52.804 --> 49:54.347
-[gentle music concludes] -[sobs softly]

719
49:58.184 --> 49:59.560
[Mi-do] For the Taegye-ri case…

720
50:00.937 --> 50:02.146
find another lawyer.

721
50:02.939 --> 50:04.023
Han Tae-seung won't do it.

722
50:12.740 --> 50:16.369
Sadly, that's not for you to decide, Director Lee Mi-do, is it?

723
50:18.287 --> 50:19.831
He likes me. Do you know why?

724
50:22.166 --> 50:23.668
Because I am a crazy bitch.

725
50:26.379 --> 50:27.338
[chuckles]

726
50:28.005 --> 50:33.386
Just out of curiosity, are you trying to play that Song Hae-na card, huh?

727
50:34.470 --> 50:35.638
I'd really be disappointed then.

728
50:35.972 --> 50:36.848
That's no fun.

729
50:41.853 --> 50:43.813
Other than Park Pil-du, leader of the Jaeseons,

730
50:45.481 --> 50:48.025
there are plenty of takers for this Song Hae-na card.

731
50:48.150 --> 50:49.694
[tense music playing]

732
50:49.819 --> 50:52.446
You and your father-in-law have a lot of guys against you.

733
50:56.826 --> 50:59.954
Don't give the Taegye-ri case to Han Tae-seung.

734
51:00.705 --> 51:01.581
I made myself clear.

735
51:03.457 --> 51:05.209
Don't give him any suspicious cases.

736
51:05.334 --> 51:08.880
Actually… just leave him the hell alone.

737
51:09.547 --> 51:10.548
Don't reach out.

738
51:14.218 --> 51:15.970
[exhales deeply]

739
51:16.095 --> 51:17.305
[chuckles]

740
51:18.389 --> 51:19.724
It's not like I look for him.

741
51:22.310 --> 51:23.352
He comes to me.

742
51:24.145 --> 51:25.396
[music rises]

743
51:25.521 --> 51:26.480
[door opens]

744
51:47.585 --> 51:49.503
Do you have any idea what you just did?

745
51:50.671 --> 51:53.507
I got caught by you while threatening Attorney Seo.

746
51:53.633 --> 51:54.508
Isn't that angering?

747
51:54.967 --> 51:59.472
You think Seo Ju-hyeok is easy because you can push me around?

748
52:00.848 --> 52:01.849
The agreement.

749
52:02.516 --> 52:04.644
I let you off easy because I really liked you.

750
52:04.769 --> 52:08.189
If I handled it like my other cases, you wouldn't even be here.

751
52:10.232 --> 52:11.359
Han Tae-seung.

752
52:11.651 --> 52:13.027
You don't have time to relax.

753
52:13.152 --> 52:14.445
Wanna go get some udon?

754
52:16.697 --> 52:18.032
Come on, let's get some udon.

755
52:27.041 --> 52:28.167
[tense music concludes]

756
52:28.292 --> 52:29.168
JEONGDAM UDON

757
52:29.293 --> 52:32.880
I promised to find out why you wander around Myeong-dong.

758
52:34.757 --> 52:35.925
[scoffs softly]

759
52:37.885 --> 52:39.679
What a great parting gift. Can't believe it.

760
52:42.348 --> 52:43.599
How long have you known?

761
52:51.941 --> 52:52.858
I asked you something.

762
52:53.275 --> 52:54.276
What?

763
52:54.735 --> 52:56.529
That this is the reason you roamed Myeong-dong?

764
52:58.948 --> 53:03.494
Or that this very udon shop turns out to be full of memories with Attorney Seo?

765
53:06.664 --> 53:10.042
Or that you love Attorney Seo so much?

766
53:10.334 --> 53:11.877
[chokes, coughs]

767
53:12.753 --> 53:13.838
Have you lost it?

768
53:14.422 --> 53:15.756
I'm crazy about women.

769
53:17.383 --> 53:18.968
I knew from the day I called you

770
53:19.635 --> 53:20.594
his lapdog…

771
53:23.055 --> 53:24.432
that you really care about that guy.

772
53:25.141 --> 53:26.100
Am I wrong?

773
53:30.104 --> 53:31.689
You seemed really sad back then.

774
53:35.359 --> 53:38.612
You handled the Taegye-ri case for his sake.

775
53:39.822 --> 53:42.366
When his father-in-law pressured Attorney Seo with that,

776
53:43.159 --> 53:45.536
you wanted to help him, so you examined the case closely.

777
53:48.122 --> 53:49.832
Come on. That's not true.

778
53:52.501 --> 53:53.544
I said it's not.

779
53:53.961 --> 53:55.046
Stop it, all right?

780
53:56.672 --> 53:59.258
I know you better than you give me credit for.

781
54:01.385 --> 54:02.470
[soft music playing]

782
54:02.595 --> 54:04.263
[Ju-hyeok] Let's get this straight, Your Honor.

783
54:05.097 --> 54:09.435
The defendant, Han Tae-seung, may indeed have killed the victim.

784
54:09.560 --> 54:10.853
That's a fact.

785
54:10.978 --> 54:15.107
[gallery gasping, murmuring]

786
54:16.233 --> 54:19.570
Yet the reason I defended him and argued for his innocence

787
54:20.446 --> 54:24.700
is that Han Tae-seung earnestly swore to me

788
54:24.950 --> 54:27.870
he was not the person who committed it.

789
54:28.412 --> 54:30.664
That's why I ask Your Honor to give

790
54:30.790 --> 54:32.500
this 16-year-old boy

791
54:32.625 --> 54:36.337
the strength to live on so that he is no longer alone.

792
54:37.171 --> 54:38.422
[music rises]

793
54:40.966 --> 54:42.593
[Mi-do] You must have missed him so much.

794
54:43.636 --> 54:45.012
The Attorney Seo you knew.

795
54:48.224 --> 54:49.350
But Tae-seung…

796
54:51.519 --> 54:52.686
Attorney Seo,

797
54:53.854 --> 54:55.231
is not here anymore.

798
54:58.526 --> 54:59.443
Wait.

799
55:00.653 --> 55:02.029
But you can see him again.

800
55:03.614 --> 55:04.782
Wanna know how?

801
55:17.169 --> 55:18.462
Try to become him.

802
55:22.299 --> 55:23.676
That first good version of him.

803
55:24.135 --> 55:25.719
That lawyer who saved you.

804
55:27.012 --> 55:28.222
You can be him.

805
55:30.224 --> 55:32.393
I'm pretty sure you were a kind kid.

806
55:36.272 --> 55:37.231
I mean it.

807
55:39.024 --> 55:41.152
You were a really, really good kid.

808
55:52.288 --> 55:53.914
[soft music concludes]

809
56:09.388 --> 56:10.598
Why did you do that?

810
56:12.933 --> 56:14.810
You didn't have to do anything.

811
56:18.314 --> 56:19.356
Why go that far?

812
56:19.982 --> 56:21.525
I wanted you to keep holding on.

813
56:24.069 --> 56:25.279
Headquarters is better for you.

814
56:26.780 --> 56:28.073
There's at least hope there.

815
56:29.617 --> 56:30.451
Hang in there.

816
56:31.076 --> 56:32.036
Grit your teeth.

817
56:35.247 --> 56:37.750
First and last time, I take the fall for you.

818
56:40.669 --> 56:42.296
So whenever you want to run away,

819
56:43.130 --> 56:45.216
remember how I'm being chipped away for you.

820
56:46.759 --> 56:49.637
And how painful it was for me, so you just keep going at all costs.

821
56:51.847 --> 56:54.516
In life, there are things you'd never do for yourself, but…

822
56:56.227 --> 56:59.480
strangely, you're willing to endure them for another one's sake.

823
57:07.488 --> 57:09.698
My biological father was a pile of trash.

824
57:12.117 --> 57:13.994
He was a famous gangster in Busan.

825
57:15.913 --> 57:18.457
And dozens of people were left disabled because of him.

826
57:21.543 --> 57:24.463
I hated having his blood in my veins and his DNA.

827
57:25.297 --> 57:26.507
It scared me a lot.

828
57:27.925 --> 57:29.009
And then…

829
57:31.053 --> 57:33.806
they say I'm good at drawing because I take after him.

830
57:37.434 --> 57:40.145
As soon as I found that out, I quit drawing.

831
57:42.690 --> 57:45.401
I hated so much carrying his genes inside.

832
57:48.612 --> 57:52.616
Giving up drawing was fair because that talent came from him.

833
57:54.034 --> 57:56.537
And having it made me feel awful.

834
58:03.627 --> 58:06.297
That's my secret and shame not even Mi-do knows.

835
58:08.757 --> 58:11.552
Su-a, I kept my promise, so now…

836
58:13.262 --> 58:14.305
you keep yours.

837
58:16.807 --> 58:18.267
Starting tomorrow, we're co-workers.

838
58:18.392 --> 58:19.268
That's it.

839
58:30.863 --> 58:32.948
[emotional music playing]

840
58:40.748 --> 58:42.333
[elevator dings]

841
58:56.013 --> 58:57.723
[music softens]

842
59:00.976 --> 59:02.102
You're completely wrong.

843
59:03.437 --> 59:04.480
I wasn't a good kid.

844
59:07.566 --> 59:09.943
You know I didn't do it just for Seo Ju-hyeok.

845
59:14.573 --> 59:16.116
I'm someone who found it easy.

846
59:17.076 --> 59:18.869
That's why I was able to do it.

847
59:20.621 --> 59:21.872
You want that?

848
59:23.290 --> 59:24.583
Then I'll give it a try.

849
59:26.794 --> 59:31.173
I'll try with everything I got to become the best version of myself.

850
59:35.094 --> 59:36.220
So I'm asking you.

851
59:41.141 --> 59:42.184
Don't leave me.

852
59:44.186 --> 59:45.104
I swear I'll be good.

853
59:47.648 --> 59:48.774
Just down leave me.

854
59:54.822 --> 59:56.782
[music rises]

855
01:00:13.215 --> 01:00:14.425
You've never held me before.

856
01:00:19.763 --> 01:00:21.723
Tell me how you can hold me while you're leaving.

857
01:00:33.902 --> 01:00:35.070
If you do this…

858
01:00:37.197 --> 01:00:38.657
how can I forget you?

859
01:00:40.492 --> 01:00:42.494
I'm the one who's really not good.

860
01:00:45.998 --> 01:00:48.417
I think I feel less guilty if I do this.

861
01:00:50.794 --> 01:00:52.171
I can forget you this way.

862
01:00:56.258 --> 01:00:57.384
I'm sorry.

863
01:01:24.578 --> 01:01:26.038
[Su-a panting]

864
01:01:27.539 --> 01:01:28.540
You have no spine.

865
01:01:30.501 --> 01:01:31.793
My hopes were so high.

866
01:01:33.962 --> 01:01:38.425
I was prepared to settle for a secret that even Miss Lee didn't know.

867
01:01:42.387 --> 01:01:43.847
You said you'd get chipped away?

868
01:01:46.016 --> 01:01:46.934
Fine.

869
01:01:47.851 --> 01:01:48.894
Then I'll do that.

870
01:01:51.188 --> 01:01:52.272
I'll be a coward.

871
01:01:53.398 --> 01:01:54.483
That promise is off.

872
01:01:56.109 --> 01:01:57.444
Even if you marry Mi-do,

873
01:01:58.070 --> 01:02:00.531
I'll keep loving you and stay right by your side.

874
01:02:18.882 --> 01:02:20.133
[emotional music concludes]

875
01:02:21.510 --> 01:02:23.011
["Stay" playing]

876
01:02:49.121 --> 01:02:50.998
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

877
01:03:04.761 --> 01:03:05.929
THANK YOU TO LEE SANG-YI FOR HIS SPECIAL APPEARANCE

878
01:03:06.138 --> 01:03:09.266
[Tae-seung] Tell me you don't miss Namgung at all.

879
01:03:09.391 --> 01:03:11.143
[Namgung] If you and I had met like ordinary people

880
01:03:11.268 --> 01:03:14.855
under other circumstances, our ending would have been different.

881
01:03:14.980 --> 01:03:17.691
[Mi-do] I just broke up with Tae-seung and came straight here.

882
01:03:17.816 --> 01:03:21.320
You're the one who taught me that life could be this happy.

883
01:03:21.445 --> 01:03:22.821
[Mi-do] Why are we such a mess?

884
01:03:23.739 --> 01:03:24.781
[Namgung] What can we do?

885
01:03:25.282 --> 01:03:26.575
That's just who we are.

886
01:03:31.455 --> 01:03:32.456
[song concludes]
